msgid "Known issues include:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 3.2.10.Final, the tenth maintenance release of the 3.2 LTS release "
"train has been released."
msgstr ""

msgid "This release includes the following security-related fixes:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-5675[CVE-2023-5675] "
"Authorization flaw in Quarkus RestEasy Reactive and Classic when \"quarkus."
"security.jaxrs.deny-unannotated-endpoints\" or \"quarkus.security.jaxrs."
"default-roles-allowed\" properties are used"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-6267[CVE-2023-6267] JSON "
"payload getting processed prior to security checks when REST resources are "
"used with annotations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-4043[CVE-2023-4043] org.eclipse."
"parsson/parsson: Denial of Service due to large number parsing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-48795[CVE-2023-48795] apache-sshd: "
"ssh: Prefix truncation attack on Binary Packet Protocol"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-22102[CVE-2023-22102] mysql-"
"connector-java: Connector/J unspecified vulnerability"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://issues.redhat.com/browse/RESTEASY-3380[RESTEASY-3380] Source "
"references exposed in RESTEasy error response"
msgstr ""

msgid "And the following component upgrades:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache commons-compress 1.24.0 -> 1.25.0"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache SSHD 2.10.0 -> 2.12.0"
msgstr ""

msgid "Eclipse Parsson 1.1.2 -> 1.1.6"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate ORM 6.2.13.Final -> 6.2.18.Final"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate Reactive 2.0.6.Final -> 2.0.8.Final"
msgstr ""

msgid "Jandex 3.1.2 -> 3.1.6"
msgstr ""

msgid "MySQL JDBC driver version 8.0.30 -> 8.2.0"
msgstr ""

msgid "RESTEasy 6.2.4.Final -> 6.2.7.Final"
msgstr ""

msgid "SmallRye Reactive Messaging 4.6.0 -> 4.6.1"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are not already using a 3.2 release, please refer to https://github."
"com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.2[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It should be a safe upgrade for anyone already using a 3.2 release. However, "
"some users may potentially run into the following couple of issues."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Using CDI interceptors to resolve multitenant OIDC configuration fails due "
"to security fix in 3.2.10.Final"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The security fix implemented in Red Hat build of Quarkus version 3.2.10."
"Final to address https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-6267[CVE-"
"2023-6267] introduced a breaking change."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This breaking change is relevant only when using multiple OIDC providers "
"with RestEasy Classic and occurs if you use Context and Dependency Injection "
"(CDI) interceptors to programmatically resolve OIDC tenant configuration "
"identifiers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Before this fix, CDI interceptors ran before authentication checks. After "
"introducing the fix, authentication occurs before CDI interceptors are "
"triggered. Therefore, using CDI interceptors to resolve multiple OIDC "
"provider configuration identifiers no longer works. RestEasy Reactive "
"applications are not affected."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Workaround: Use the `quarkus.oidc.TenantResolver` method to resolve the "
"current OIDC configuration tenant ID."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the https://quarkus.io/version/3.2/guides/security-"
"openid-connect-multitenancy#resolving-tenant-identifiers-with-"
"annotations[Resolving tenant identifiers with annotations] section of the "
"Quarkus “Using OpenID Connect (OIDC) multitenancy” guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Change of the MySQL JDBC driver Maven artifact groupId and artifactId"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As a consequence of fixing https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-"
"22102[CVE-2023-22102], the groupId and artifactId of the MySQL JDBC driver "
"in the `quarkus-bom` has changed from"
msgstr ""

msgid "to"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Projects consuming it as a dependency of `io.quarkus:quarkus-jdbc-mysql` "
"will not be affected by this change. However, projects that had a direct "
"dependency on `mysql:mysql-connector-java` relying on `quarkus-bom` to "
"manage its version will have to update the groupId and artifactId to the new "
"ones mentioned above."
msgstr ""

